+  "de": "German softens a plain statement with particles (das funktioniert so wohl nicht), but the particles disappear in translation and that doesn't work remains. English needs a lexical hedge instead: I don't think that's going to work.",
+  "it": "Non credo che funzioni corresponds exactly to I don't think it'll work, with the negation in the same place. The hedge therefore transfers directly.",
+  "fr": "Je ne pense pas que ça marche corresponds exactly to I don't think it'll work, with the negation in the same place. The hedge therefore transfers directly.",
